#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323248 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186321497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323248 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "276fef95-8127-5751-a8f3-63d27774306c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=1$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,j$ and $r(t)=(2{t}^{2}+2)\\,i+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,j.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fdba027b-12bc-5b22-aa20-f040a6af0b36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323880 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,i+\\frac{1}{y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=2{t}^{2}+2$ and $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}+2}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =4t\\,i+\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}+2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (4t\\,i+\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{t}^{2}+2}\\cdot 4t+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{({t}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t+1}{({t}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =\\frac{2(1)\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1+1}{({1}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+1)}{(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi +2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358067 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358067 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358067 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23b55c69-c88a-5b54-9cd7-12d2acc90eba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358206 #edb/ref 1080 "2-3{e}^{-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358206 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358206 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "336ae663-8acc-530e-96cc-0c9939efc8b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358354 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8}{13}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358354 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358354 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46655cc2-46c6-57d9-aae7-530ec487a9e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358429 #edb/ref 1080 "3e+{e}^{-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358429 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358429 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4e8323a2-f87f-54c1-ba41-37494660f68d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358466 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+{e}^{{t}^{2}}+t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358466 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358466 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5305687e-83d8-5c87-af7d-a5b0a362d788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358573 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{12}{17}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5de3fd27-1a74-5e78-9c11-0753f0b2af77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358613 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{csc}⁡t+2t{e}^{{t}^{2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218635861