#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485588 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)$ and $r(t)=(t+1)\\,i+2t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eabe5e6a-dc85-5118-84d2-9aa9f31a6a23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485588 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z))\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+z)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t+1,$ $y=2t$ and $z={t}^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+2\\,j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,j+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\,k)\\cdot (\\,i+2\\,j+2t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 1+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 2+(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2t(t+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)(1+t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{t}^{2})+2(t+1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186485633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2989f12e-e4d2-5eea-a076-313f05f3b144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485611 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186485608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485611 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3232ec86-62d5-5c61-ba3f-93622480e150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485611 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485628 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a35955fa-8e05-5fc2-9647-6f1fbb5eff50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485628 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186485611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb7a2b36-6b63-51f3-9376-761d5f709c35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485631 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485633 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186485628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bd21bb0d-0ac3-5b0d-8a0d-e84c7b42e305" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186485588 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
